id:attributionCreator rdf:type prov:Attribution .
id:attributionDataManager rdf:type prov:Attribution .
id:attributionInvestigator rdf:type prov:Attribution .
id:attributionProjectAdministrator rdf:type prov:Attribution .
id:cc dct:identifier <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/> .
id:cc rdf:type dct:LicenseDocument .
id:concept1OfDataset dct:description "psychological"@en .
id:concept1OfDataset rdf:type skos:Concept .
id:concept2OfDataset dct:description "lay people’s and philosophers’ susceptibility"@en .
id:concept2OfDataset rdf:type skos:Concept .
id:concept3OfDataset dct:description " Demographic data "@en .
id:concept3OfDataset rdf:type skos:Concept .
id:dataIdentifier datacite:usesIdentifierScheme datacite:doi .
id:dataIdentifier rdf:type datacite:Identifier .
id:dataProvenance dct:description "Most of the project’s empirical studies will be designed in Qualtrics, an online survey software. Participants of the studies will be recruited from online crowdsourcing pools such as Prolific Academic, mostly in the US. For their time and effort all participants will be compensated at an hourly rate that is above the national minimal income."@en .
id:dataProvenance rdf:type dct:ProvenanceStatement .
id:dataProvenanceStandard dct:description "the common standards in psychology and experimental philosophy, i.e., studies will be reported in a journal article which involves a dedicated “Participants” section, specifying how participants were recruited, what number of participants were recruited, why this number of participants was recruited, who the participants were (demographic data), etc."@en .
id:dataProvenanceStandard rdf:type dct:Standard .
id:dataset dct:description "The data may include qualified references to other data that has been collected in the project. If this is the case (for example, if follow-up studies are conducted to be better able to evaluate explanations of data or cross-cultural research is conducted to test previous findings’ generalizability across different countries) then the scientific links between the datasets will be described on OSF as well as in the resulting pre-prints and journal articles."@en .
id:dataset rdf:type schema11:Thing .
id:dataset rdf:type dcat:Dataset .
id:datasetAccessProtocol rdf:type schema11:EntryPoint .
id:datasetAccessibility rdf:type dmp:Access .
id:datasetAvailability rdf:type dmp:Availability .
id:datasetAvailabilityDuration rdf:type dct:PeriodOfTime .
id:datasetAvailabilityDuration dmp:minimumDuration "At least ten years"@en .
id:datasetEmbargo rdf:type dmp:Embargo .
id:datasetInformedConsent dct:description "Yes, each study will involve a consent page. Participants will be asked to agree to the following claims before they can complete the studies: I agree that my personal data (including demographic information), which is collected anonymously during this study, is processed by the University of Graz by means of statistical data analysis for research purposes and used to publish scientific papers. I agree that my anonymized data will be made available in open databases (e.g. in the Open Science Framework; https://osf.io/) indefinitely for the purpose of scientific transparency. I can withdraw my consent to the processing of my data at any time by writing to Dr. Thomas Pölzler, thomas.poelzler@uni-graz.at, University of Graz, Attemsgasse 25/II, 8010 Graz. The revocation does not affect the legality of the data processed until the revocation. I have read the above instructions and I agree to participate. I know that I can cancel my participation at any time without giving reasons"@en .
id:datasetInformedConsent rdf:type dmp:InformedConsent .
id:datasetPreservation rdf:type dmp:Preservation .
id:datasetPreservationDuration rdf:type dct:PeriodOfTime .
id:datasetPreservationDuration dmp:minimumDuration "At least ten years"@en .
id:datasetSecurityPrivacy dct:description "  If the project collects sensitive data then this data will be sufficiently anonymized before being uploaded to OSF. The original sensitive data, stored on the USB flash drive, will be password protected. It can only be accessed by the project leader and co-authors who have collaborated in generating and analysing the data."@en .
id:datasetSecurityPrivacy rdf:type dcso:SecurityPrivacy .
